{"name":"Provence Blue","hex":"#8a9c99","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Provence","blocks":[{"text":"Provence is a geographical, cultural region and historical province of southeastern France, which stretches from the left bank of the lower Rhône to the west to the Italian border to the east; it is bordered by the Mediterranean Sea to the south. It largely corresponds with the modern administrative region of Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur and includes the departments of Var, Bouches-du-Rhône, Alpes-de-Haute-Provence, as well as parts of Alpes-Maritimes and Vaucluse. The largest city of the region and its modern-day capital is Marseille."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Lavender_field_and_Mont_Ventoux.jpg/330px-Lavender_field_and_Mont_Ventoux.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Provence","wikidata":"Q101081"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Provence_in_France_%281789_borders_over_modern_Provence%29.png/500px-Provence_in_France_%281789_borders_over_modern_Provence%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Provence_in_France_%281789_borders_over_modern_Provence%29.png/1280px-Provence_in_France_%281789_borders_over_modern_Provence%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Provence_in_France_%281789_borders_over_modern_Provence%29.png/500px-Provence_in_France_%281789_borders_over_modern_Provence%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AProvence_in_France_(1789_borders_over_modern_Provence).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/PACA.jpg/500px-PACA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/PACA.jpg/500px-PACA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The historical province of Provence (orange) within the contemporary region of Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur in southeastern France","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APACA.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Cours_Mirabeau_from_the_air_in_Aix_en_Provence.jpg/500px-Cours_Mirabeau_from_the_air_in_Aix_en_Provence.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign